{
  "abstract": "Zero-dependency Lean 4 formalization of two results of Erdős and Gyárfás (1999) associated with Erdős Problem #617: (1) for every prime p — and consequently for arbitrarily large primes p >= N by Euclid's theorem — the complete graph K_{p^2} admits a symmetric balanced p-coloring where every (p + 1)-subset contains edges of all p colors, constructed via finite affine planes AG(2, p); and (2) every symmetric 3-coloring of K_10 contains a 4-vertex subset missing at least one color, proved via a single-color diamond-free extremal degree and triangle-counting argument.",
